# The suite's static-analysis level. D00 T01 §3.
#
# The set is deliberately narrower than "everything". A check list nobody can
# get to zero is a list somebody turns off, and this one is attached to a
# ratchet (`todo/.tidy-baseline`) that only moves down.
#
# What is in: the families that find defects rather than style opinions.
#   bugprone-*        real mistakes: misuse, narrowing, dangling, bad casts
#   clang-analyzer-*  path-sensitive analysis: leaks, null derefs, uninit reads
#   performance-*     copies and conversions that cost something
#   misc-*            the leftovers that are still defects
#
# What is out, and why, so the next person does not re-litigate it:
#   modernize-*       churn across the whole intake for no behavioural gain
#   readability-*     style, and DESIGN.md is where style is decided
#   *-magic-numbers   a Direct2D surface is made of them
#   misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes  the control structs are PODs
#   misc-include-cleaner  reports Win32 umbrella headers as unused
#   misc-const-correctness  see below
#
# `misc-const-correctness` is excluded on the same defects-not-style principle,
# and it is called out because the number is startling. It alone accounted for
# 524 of 577 findings on the first run, 91 percent, all of them "this local
# could be const". A baseline that is nine parts one style check is a baseline
# where a real regression is invisible, which is the opposite of what the
# ratchet in D07 T01 §2 is for. Re-enabling it is a decision to make const a
# suite-wide convention and fix 524 sites, not a config tweak.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  misc-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace,
  -misc-const-correctness,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -bugprone-magic-numbers

# Our code only. A dependency is not ours to fix, which is the same rule the
# warning policy states: `cmake/ResoluteWarnings.cmake`.
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\](src|shared)[/\].*'

WarningsAsErrors: ''
FormatStyle: none
